    description: "F66.A4 (blind severity 3/Moderate; CORRECTED-kept-as-record; F79.A1 prevalence EXTENSION folded here). A reverse slice of a heavily-called symbol hits max_files=100, reports limits_hit=[file_limit], and echoes query.max_files (100) — but the feature JSON records NO separate 'you got 100 of N' signal: no count of dropped callers, no total (slice.py:733-735). A consumer sees a populated slice + a file_limit flag but cannot tell it is missing callers without independently recomputing in-degree from the global graph. F79.A1 quantified prevalence: 13/282 high-in-degree in-repo symbols truncate at default max_files=100; 4/13 lose >50% of caller-FILES (Symbol 66%, Edge 60%, Span 60%, Edge.create 52%); Edge.create drops 169/557 callers (30%), 107/207 caller-files (52%). An agent auditing 'every caller of X' to validate a signature change may trust an incomplete caller set. Fix: truncated slice carries the shortfall magnitude (dropped-count or total-callers field) alongside the cap value. filed via tranch 04 (methodology-comparability run, reused tranch-03 substrate sha a32c4a31)."  # c50b
    fields: {}  # c50b
