  set:  # 1a56
    title: "truncated slice signals file_limit / hub_pruned flags but not the shortfall magnitude (no dropped/total count)"  # 1a56
    description: "F66.A4 (blind severity 3/Moderate; CORRECTED-kept-as-record; F79.A1 prevalence EXTENSION folded here). A reverse slice of a heavily-called symbol hits max_files=100, reports limits_hit=[file_limit], and echoes query.max_files (100) — but the feature JSON records NO separate 'you got 100 of N' signal: no count of dropped callers, no total. slice.py:832-834 appends \"file_limit\" and skips the node without counting it; SliceResult / to_dict (slice.py:320-374) carry entry_nodes, node_ids, edge_ids, query, limits_hit, node_depths, node_tiers, admission_stats only, and the CLI summary (cli.py:2170-2177) prints nodes/edges/\"limits hit\". The same holds for hub_pruned (slice.py:707-708): a second truncation flag with no magnitude. A consumer sees a populated slice + a flag but cannot tell how much is missing without independently recomputing in-degree from the global graph.\n\nMeasured on a self-analysis map of this repo (dev 134a06d505, 55,141 nodes / 217,668 edges): `slice --entry Edge.create --reverse` (defaults) -> limits_hit [file_limit, hub_pruned]; 316 of 656 direct callers dropped (48%), 138 of 237 caller files dropped (58%). F79.A1's prevalence census (13/282 high-in-degree symbols truncate at max_files=100; 4/13 lose >50% of caller files) was measured at filing and not re-measured. An agent auditing 'every caller of X' to validate a signature change may trust an incomplete caller set.\n\nFix: a truncated slice carries the shortfall magnitude per limit hit (dropped count or total, for file_limit AND hub_pruned) alongside the cap value. Filed via tranch 04 (methodology-comparability run, reused tranch-03 substrate sha a32c4a31).\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 1a56
- op: discuss  # 3884
  at: '2026-10-02T00:33:54Z'  # 3884
  by: agent  # 3884
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3884
  clock: 5  # 3884
  nonce: '3884'  # 3884
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (concurrent run, agent mibuj). Local branch jgstern-agent/fix/mibuj in worktree ~/hg_wt/mibuj, commit 282958d48c (not pushed, no PR). Status unchanged.\n\nPremise re-verified: origin/dev af8ff42ad0 slice.py appended file_limit / hub_pruned to limits_hit with no count; fixture repro (target() called from 6 files, `slice --entry target --reverse --max-files 3`) emitted feature keys edge_ids, entry_nodes, id, limits_hit, name, node_depths, node_ids, node_tiers, query -- no magnitude.\n\nChange: SliceResult.limits_detail -- one entry per name in limits_hit (equal key sets; absent when limits_hit is empty) with cap, nodes_omitted, edges_omitted, files_omitted, plus nodes_not_expanded for hop_limit / hub_pruned. All four limits are sized (file_limit, hub_pruned, hop_limit, tier_limit). Hub/hop shortfall is sized by a probe that runs the same per-edge filters (confidence, structural, imports, dataflow, tests, utility, tier) without touching admission_stats. Counts = the frontier the limit refused that is absent from the final slice; a LOWER BOUND (nothing beyond an omitted node was walked). CLI summary prints one magnitude line per limit. Spec features[] + docs/schema.json updated.\n\nEvidence: green targeted smart-test on 282958d48c -- 18941 passed, 0 failed, 100% coverage on the 3 changed sources (576 test files). Red run against origin/dev slice.py/cli.py -- 10/10 new TestLimitsDetail tests + test_cmd_slice_with_limits_hit FAILED. Self-survey of origin/dev af8ff42ad0 (`slice --input self.json --entry Edge.create --reverse`, defaults): limits_hit [file_limit, hub_pruned]; file_limit cap 100: 1315 nodes / 1440 edges / 204 files omitted; hub_pruned cap 50: 2 not expanded, 56 nodes / 153 edges / 7 files omitted. Independent replication from the map + slice output reproduced all 7 counts exactly. Direct-caller metric unchanged from the premise check: 656 direct calls-callers, 340 in slice, 316 dropped; 237 caller files, 99 in slice, 138 dropped.\n\nNOT done: the F79.A1 prevalence census (13/282) was not re-measured. nodes_omitted is not \"direct callers dropped\" -- it includes the deeper frontier and file nodes reached through imports edges (1315 vs 316 here)."  # 3884
